{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981898-time-magic","id":981898,"title":"Time Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-04T18:54:49-07:00","id":981898,"title":"Time Magic","content":"Alright so having a bit of a debate and would like further input. Can time magic harm a Vampire since they are a immortal creature. I know time can harm other supernatural beings who are not immune to time. This came up in our game a few days go and people said yes &amp; no so now I'm wondering were other people stand on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12294-haloth","name":"Haloth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12294_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T18:59:35-07:00","id":981899,"title":"","content":"Interesting question.<br /> <br /> In looking up some Time magic, I see under Weight of Years, ' At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, immortal creatures like vampires might be immune to the damaging properties of this spell.' With similar statements under Rend Lifespan, adding ghosts.<br /> <br /> I would certainly rule that they were immune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T19:00:22-07:00","id":981900,"title":"","content":"Depends on what you're trying to do to them with your time magic. Vampires should not, in my opinion, be immune to any and all effects of the Time Arcanum. But, direct damage spells like Weight of Years and Rend Lifespan shouldn't damage them. In fact, Weight of Years and Rend Lifespan even say, &quot;At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, undead beings like vampires and ghosts may be immune to this spell.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T19:04:54-07:00","id":981903,"title":"","content":"I'd say it does because I'm aging the body using magic, not the actual chronological passage of time. Also, from what I know of ChroDs vampires, the stop aging, not age but never change. So artificially aging the body would still have an effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T23:09:48-07:00","id":981979,"title":"","content":"As has been said, it depends on exactly how you're attacking them with it. I can see why Rend Lifespan may or might not be applicable, but as with all other aspects of the various arcana, the means of accomplishing a specific task can be pretty open ended. So sure, while Rend Lifespan might not work as a direct damage spell, a differently flavored Time spell might work perfectly fine. For example, using Time to (re)impose a past or (potential) future injury on them should work perfectly fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:33:28-07:00","id":982228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981898-time-magic?p=981903#post981903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say it does because I'm aging the body using magic, not the actual chronological passage of time. Also, from what I know of ChroDs vampires, the stop aging, not age but never change. So artificially aging the body would still have an effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the medium of that magic is manipulating the passage of time. A million years would not cause a vampire's cells to age noticeably - that's a function of their own magic. Time sets the age of the cell, and the age of the cell is irrelevant to the damage on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T12:56:59-07:00","id":982280,"title":"","content":"I like a vampire absorbing the attack with their blood pool or only getting to Clash if they reflexively spend a blood point better than straight-up immunity.<br /> Hitting a vampire while awake might increase their age for purposes of Blood Potency improvement if they are awake and win a clash. Asleep, it might count as torpor, so reduce Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> <br /> As noted repeatedly, though, the official RAW stance <i>is</i> &quot;Yo, ST: Got a job for you.&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T03:48:02-07:00","id":982632,"title":"","content":"I am thinking... if you age a Vampire, say 200 years, with Time magic, wouldn't that increase his blood potency?<br /> <br /> At the discretion of the storyteller, of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T07:08:00-07:00","id":982674,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was thinking exactly the same. It would be a nice surprise to the mage that tries to age the vampire, and as a result he becames more powerful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:02:43-07:00","id":983012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981898-time-magic?p=982632#post982632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am thinking... if you age a Vampire, say 200 years, with Time magic, wouldn't that increase his blood potency?<br /> <br /> At the discretion of the storyteller, of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Argle blargle game balance.<br /> <br /> A cute idea may be to allow that, but the shock of it sends him into a no-save Frenzy.<br /> <br /> And probably still cannot be made Lasting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T18:02:49-07:00","id":983049,"title":"","content":"If it's cast as a damaging spell then the &quot;damage&quot; of aging would be Lasting by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T22:25:22-07:00","id":983158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dourden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981898-time-magic?p=982632#post982632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am thinking... if you age a Vampire, say 200 years, with Time magic, wouldn't that increase his blood potency?<br /> <br /> At the discretion of the storyteller, of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you do it enough, they would have to feed on Kindred (or use Willpower), could be used to reek havoc on their (un)life and the All Night Society in general. Also, if you do then send them to Torpor somehow it would be for a long time. Might be good revenge on them for something that Final Death would be to easy on them for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T01:20:08-07:00","id":983212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981898-time-magic?p=981899#post981899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting question.<br /> <br /> In looking up some Time magic, I see under Weight of Years, ' At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, immortal creatures like vampires might be immune to the damaging properties of this spell.' With similar statements under Rend Lifespan, adding ghosts.<br /> <br /> I would certainly rule that they were immune.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make it drain their Vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/191-strill","name":"Strill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T08:23:10-07:00","id":983333,"title":"","content":"If the basic premise of CoD is that average folks are aware that the supernatural exists, I'd presume that a more highly experienced mage would take from nearly every representation of vampires over the years that such beings were effectively immortal, and so would avoid trying to prematurely age such a being in the first place.<br /> <br /> Kill it with fire. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:43:52-07:00","id":983374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Strill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981898-time-magic?p=983212#post983212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would make it drain their Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what my wife said, due to the needing a Vitae to wake up every day. But if you don't go to sleep you don't need to use that Vitae, and if you're just zipping time around the vampire, the sun isn't rising and setting above them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Midgardener</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/981898-time-magic?p=983333#post983333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the basic premise of CoD is that average folks are aware that the supernatural exists, I'd presume that a more highly experienced mage would take from nearly every representation of vampires over the years that such beings were effectively immortal, and so would avoid trying to prematurely age such a being in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might not have been identified as a vampire in the first place. And presumably the reason it's up to the Storyteller is because some will have magic 'trump' vampire immortality, or some will not be using Requiem rules and perhaps have vampires that aren't truly immortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}